{"kind": "question", "qid": "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf#0", "hops": 1, "gold_answer": "Berlin School of Experimental Psychology", "answer": "Gestalt psychology was conceived in the Berlin School of Experimental Psychology. The slide states: \"Gestalt psychology was conceived in the Berlin School of Experimental Psychology, and tries to understand the laws of our ability to acquire and maintain meaningful perceptions.\" It also notes the German origin of the term Gestalt (German: Gestalt [\u0261\u0259\u02c8\u0283talt] \"shape, form\").", "citations": [{"doc_id": "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf", "page": 1, "bbox": {"x0": 0.043, "y0": 0.247, "x1": 0.945, "y1": 0.312}}, {"doc_id": "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf", "page": 1, "bbox": {"x0": 0.054, "y0": 0.428, "x1": 0.538, "y1": 0.478}}], "ranked": ["0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p001", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p010", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p002", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p007", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p000"], "pool": ["0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p001", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p010", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p002", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p007", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p000"], "ndcg_at_k": 1.0, "recall_at_k": 1.0, "pool_recall": 1.0, "iou_at_threshold": 1.0, "bbox_hit_rate": 1.0, "rounds": 1, "calls": 4, "tokens": 13032, "stop_reason": "", "latency_s": 5.552}
{"kind": "question", "qid": "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf#1", "hops": 1, "gold_answer": "21%", "answer": "Based on the chart titled \"Time spent on weekends\" on page 14, the time spent with family and friends in 2010 was 21%. The chart compares 2005 and 2010, showing that the 2005 value for this category was 35%, while the 2010 value dropped to 21%.", "citations": [{"doc_id": "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf", "page": 13, "bbox": {"x0": 0.6, "y0": 0.38, "x1": 0.68, "y1": 0.52}}], "ranked": ["0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p013", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p011", "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p017", "watch_d/p021", "watch_d/p022"], "pool": ["0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p013", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p011", "watch_d/p021", "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p017", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p007", "2023.acl-long.386/p017", "2023.acl-long.386/p023", "2023.acl-long.386/p021", "2023.acl-long.386/p019", "2023.acl-long.386/p022", "2023.acl-long.386/p018", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p014", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p004", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p006", "watch_d/p001", "2023.acl-long.386/p006", "watch_d/p006", "2023.acl-long.386/p014", "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p004", "watch_d/p018", "2023.acl-long.386/p003", "watch_d/p015", "2023.acl-long.386/p002"], "ndcg_at_k": 1.0, "recall_at_k": 1.0, "pool_recall": 1.0, "iou_at_threshold": 1.0, "bbox_hit_rate": 1.0, "rounds": 5, "calls": 14, "tokens": 156520, "stop_reason": "recover_exhausted", "latency_s": 99.19}
{"kind": "question", "qid": "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf#2", "hops": 1, "gold_answer": "0-375 miles", "answer": "In the \"Tracking the West Nile Virus\" chart, the red color in the legend titled \"Approximate Distance from the Mississippi River (miles)\" represents 0 - 375 miles.", "citations": [{"doc_id": "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf", "page": 9, "bbox": {"x0": 0.585, "y0": 0.665, "x1": 0.625, "y1": 0.7}}], "ranked": ["0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p009", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p005", "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p009", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p008", "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p008"], "pool": ["0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p009", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p008", "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p008", "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p018", "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p009", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p011", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p005"], "ndcg_at_k": 1.0, "recall_at_k": 1.0, "pool_recall": 1.0, "iou_at_threshold": 1.0, "bbox_hit_rate": 1.0, "rounds": 1, "calls": 4, "tokens": 17031, "stop_reason": "", "latency_s": 7.571}
{"kind": "question", "qid": "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf#3", "hops": 1, "gold_answer": "Elements of objects tend to be perceptually grouped together if they form a pattern that is regular, simple, and orderly.", "answer": "According to the document, the Law of good Gestalt is defined as follows: \"Elements of objects tend to be perceptually grouped together if they form a pattern that is regular, simple, and orderly.\" The document further explains that this law implies that as individuals perceive the world, they eliminate complexity and unfamiliarity so they can observe a reality in its most simplistic form, and that eliminating extraneous stimuli helps the mind create meaning. It adds that the meaning created by perception implies a global regularity, which is often mentally prioritized over spatial relations, and that the law of good gestalt focuses on the idea of conciseness, which is what all of gestalt theory is based on.", "citations": [{"doc_id": "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf", "page": 10, "bbox": {"x0": 0.041, "y0": 0.239, "x1": 0.492, "y1": 0.478}}, {"doc_id": "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf", "page": 10, "bbox": {"x0": 0.041, "y0": 0.525, "x1": 0.496, "y1": 0.669}}], "ranked": ["0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p010", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p001", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p002", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p007", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p000"], "pool": ["0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p010", "2023.acl-long.386/p000", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p001", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p002", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p007", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p000", "2023.acl-long.386/p006"], "ndcg_at_k": 1.0, "recall_at_k": 1.0, "pool_recall": 1.0, "iou_at_threshold": 1.0, "bbox_hit_rate": 1.0, "rounds": 1, "calls": 4, "tokens": 17262, "stop_reason": "", "latency_s": 6.873}
{"kind": "question", "qid": "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf#4", "hops": 1, "gold_answer": "Eating out", "answer": "Based on the \"Time spent on weekends\" chart comparing 2005 and 2010, \"With family and friends\" is the category with the largest decrease, dropping from 35% in 2005 to 21% in 2010 \u2014 a decline of 14 percentage points, the biggest change of any category. Among the categories that increased, eating out (10% to 17%) and \"people who start their own business\" (4% to 10%) each rose, but no category shows an increase as large as 14 points; the largest increase is 7 points (eating out), so if the question is about the largest increase, the answer would be eating out (10%\u219217%), while the largest overall change is the decrease in \"with family and friends\" (35%\u219221%).", "citations": [{"doc_id": "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf", "page": 13, "bbox": {"x0": 0.29, "y0": 0.31, "x1": 0.72, "y1": 0.72}}], "ranked": ["0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p013", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p014", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p006", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p005", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p011"], "pool": ["0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p013", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p006", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p014", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p003", "2023.acl-long.386/p013", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p011", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p005", "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p004", "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p016", "2023.acl-long.386/p017", "watch_d/p021", "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p017", "watch_d/p001", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p012", "2023.acl-long.386/p015", "watch_d/p011", "2023.acl-long.386/p006", "2023.acl-long.386/p007", "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p009", "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p008", "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p011", "2023.acl-long.386/p009", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p008", "2023.acl-long.386/p002", "2023.acl-long.386/p021", "2023.