{"kind": "question", "qid": "watch_d#0", "hops": 1, "gold_answer": "8", "answer": "The guidebook demonstrates 9 (nine) incorrect postures for measuring blood pressure. On the page titled \"Incorrect postures when measuring blood pressure,\" there is a set of nine illustrated figures, each showing a person in a different wrong position with an \"\u2715\" mark beneath it \u2014 arranged in three rows of three (three figures in the top row, three in the middle row, and three in the bottom row). Each of these nine figures is marked with an \u2715 to indicate that the posture is incorrect.", "citations": [{"doc_id": "watch_d", "page": 14, "bbox": {"x0": 0.092, "y0": 0.183, "x1": 0.458, "y1": 0.469}}], "ranked": ["watch_d/p014", "watch_d/p012", "watch_d/p013", "watch_d/p001", "watch_d/p016"], "pool": ["watch_d/p012", "watch_d/p014", "watch_d/p011", "watch_d/p013", "watch_d/p001", "2023.acl-long.386/p007", "2023.acl-long.386/p016", "2023.acl-long.386/p006", "watch_d/p006", "watch_d/p005", "watch_d/p018", "watch_d/p015", "2023.acl-long.386/p004", "2023.acl-long.386/p015", "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p017", "2023.acl-long.386/p005", "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p013", "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p008", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p007", "2023.acl-long.386/p008", "2023.acl-long.386/p020", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p002", "watch_d/p016", "watch_d/p019", "2023.acl-long.386/p012", "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p001", "2023.acl-long.386/p010", "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p003", "watch_d/p022", "watch_d/p009"], "ndcg_at_k": 1.0, "recall_at_k": 1.0, "pool_recall": 1.0, "iou_at_threshold": 1.0, "bbox_hit_rate": 1.0, "rounds": 5, "calls": 15, "tokens": 212164, "stop_reason": "budget_exhausted", "latency_s": 56.04}
{"kind": "question", "qid": "watch_d#1", "hops": 1, "gold_answer": "2.5-3cm", "answer": "According to the figure on page 4, the \"two fingers' distance\" (from the bottom of your palm to where the ruler end is placed) is labeled as **2.5\u20133 cm**. The illustrations show the wrist with the ruler looped through the buckle, annotated with the red measurement \"2.5\u20133 cm\" in both the strap-threading and completed illustrations.\n\nThis matches the instruction: \"At a position on your wrist that is about the width of two fingers away from the bottom of your palm, put the end of the ruler that comes with the watch through the buckle on the head.\"", "citations": [{"doc_id": "watch_d", "page": 5, "bbox": {"x0": 0.14, "y0": 0.3, "x1": 0.6, "y1": 0.44}}, {"doc_id": "watch_d", "page": 5, "bbox": {"x0": 0.08, "y0": 0.62, "x1": 0.72, "y1": 0.66}}], "ranked": ["watch_d/p005", "watch_d/p006", "watch_d/p003", "watch_d/p002", "watch_d/p007"], "pool": ["watch_d/p005", "watch_d/p006", "watch_d/p002", "watch_d/p001", "watch_d/p007", "watch_d/p019", "watch_d/p022", "watch_d/p013"], "ndcg_at_k": 1.0, "recall_at_k": 1.0, "pool_recall": 1.0, "iou_at_threshold": 1.0, "bbox_hit_rate": 1.0, "rounds": 1, "calls": 4, "tokens": 19504, "stop_reason": "", "latency_s": 7.088}
{"kind": "question", "qid": "watch_d#2", "hops": 1, "gold_answer": "2", "answer": "Two steps are needed to customize the function of the Down button.\n\nStep 1: Press the Up button to open the app list and then go to **Settings** > **Down button** (watch_d/p008).\n\nStep 2: Select an app and customize the function of the Down button; after you have finished customizing the function, return to the home screen and press the Down button to open the current app (watch_d/p009).", "citations": [{"doc_id": "watch_d", "page": 8, "bbox": {"x0": 0.046, "y0": 0.894, "x1": 0.927, "y1": 0.923}}, {"doc_id": "watch_d", "page": 9, "bbox": {"x0": 0.046, "y0": 0.07, "x1": 0.872, "y1": 0.132}}], "ranked": ["watch_d/p009", "watch_d/p008", "watch_d/p002", "watch_d/p001", "watch_d/p023"], "pool": ["watch_d/p008", "watch_d/p009", "watch_d/p002", "watch_d/p001", "watch_d/p023"], "ndcg_at_k": 1.0, "recall_at_k": 1.0, "pool_recall": 1.0, "iou_at_threshold": 1.0, "bbox_hit_rate": 1.0, "rounds": 1, "calls": 4, "tokens": 14213, "stop_reason": "", "latency_s": 7.85}
{"kind": "question", "qid": "watch_d#3", "hops": 1, "gold_answer": "Wake up the voice assistant. ", "answer": "Pressing and holding the Down button **wakes up the voice assistant**. Note that the voice assistant is only supported in some countries/regions.\n\nThe Down button table on the \"Buttons and screen control\" page lists two operations:\n- **Press once**: The Blood pressure app is enabled by default; or access the set customized feature. (There are certain exceptions such as for calls and workouts.)\n- **Press and hold**: Wake up the voice assistant. (Voice assistant is only supported in some countries/regions.)", "citations": [{"doc_id": "watch_d", "page": 2, "bbox": {"x0": 0.06, "y0": 0.62, "x1": 0.95, "y1": 0.85}}], "ranked": ["watch_d/p010", "watch_d/p002", "watch_d/p025", "watch_d/p013", "watch_d/p008"], "pool": ["watch_d/p003", "watch_d/p008", "watch_d/p025", "watch_d/p023", "watch_d/p013", "watch_d/p002", "watch_d/p009", "watch_d/p001"], "ndcg_at_k": 0.6309, "recall_at_k": 1.0, "pool_recall": 1.0, "iou_at_threshold": 1.0, "bbox_hit_rate": 1.0, "rounds": 1, "calls": 4, "tokens": 19270, "stop_reason": "", "latency_s": 6.448}
{"kind": "question", "qid": "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763#0", "hops": 1, "gold_answer": "2009-07", "answer": "The date mentioned on the second page is 2023-07.\n\nSpecifically, the footnote on the second page of the paper (page 6981) states that it is from the \"Proceedings of the 61st Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics, Volume 1: Long Papers, pages 6981\u20137004, July 9-14, 2023\" (2023.acl-long.386/p000).", "citations": [{"doc_id": "2023.acl-long.386", "page": 0, "bbox": {"x0": 0.257, "y0": 0.924, "x1": 0.742, "y1": 0.965}}], "ranked": ["0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p010", "2023.acl-long.386/p016", "2023.acl-long.386/p015", "2023.acl-long.386/p018", "watch_d/p025"], "pool": ["0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p010", "watch_d/p025", "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p005", "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p001", "2023.acl-long.386/p018", "2023.acl-long.386/p001", "2023.acl-long.386/p020", "watch_d/p007", "watch_d/p024", "2023.acl-long.386/p000", "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p014", "2023.acl-long.386/p022", "2023.acl-long.386/p008", "2023.acl-long.386/p009", "2023.acl-long.386/p012", "2023.acl-long.386/p013", "watch_d/p001", "2023.acl-long.386/p011", "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p006", "2023.acl-long.386/p004", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p007", "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p011", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p014", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p008", "2023.acl-long.386/p003", "2023.acl-long.386/p007", "2023.acl-long.386/p002", "2023.acl-long.386/p010"], "ndcg_at_k": 0.0, "recall_at_k": 0.0, "pool_recall": 0.0, "iou_at_threshold": 0.0, "bbox_hit_rate": 0.0, "rounds": 5, "calls": 16, "tokens": 184648, "stop_reason": "recover_exhausted", "latency_s": 51.165}
{"kind": "question", "qid": "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763#1", "hops": 1, "gold_answer": "['combshj@unk.edu']", "answer": "The email address on the second cover page is **combshj@unk.edu**.\n\nThis appears on the title page of the Hamilton County, Nebraska Historic Buildings Survey report, listed under the preparers' contact information (H. Jason Combs (PI), Anne M. Bauer, John T. Bauer) at 501 West 28th Street, Kearney, Nebraska 68845, phone (308) 236-5137, July 2009.", "citations": [{"doc_id": "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763", "page": 2, "bbox": {"x0": 0.414, "y0": 0.585, "x1": 0.588, "y1": 0.604}}], "ranked": ["2023.acl-long.386/p009", "2023.acl-long.386/p007", "watch_d/p025", "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p002", "2023.acl-long.386/p015"], "pool": ["2023.acl-long.386/p009", "2023.acl-long.386/p012", "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p004", "2023.acl-long.386/p018", "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p005", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p010", "2023.acl-long.386/p014", "watch_d/p007", "watch_d/p025", "watch_d/p000", "2023.acl-long.386/p015", "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p002", "2023.acl-long.386/p023", "watch_d/p021", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p009", "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p000", "2023.acl-long.386/p013", "watch_d/p004", "watch_d/p009", "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p010", "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p015", "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p006"], "ndcg_at_k": 0.4307, "recall_at_k": 1.0, "pool_recall": 1.0, "iou_at_threshold": 1.0, "bbox_hit_rate": 1.0, "rounds": 4, "calls": 11, "tokens": 134843, "stop_reason": "", "latency_s": 34.467}
{"kind": "question", "qid": "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763#2", "hops": 1, "gold_answer": "538", "answer": "Hamilton County covers approximately 538 square miles. Rounded to the nearest integer, that is 538 square miles. The figure cited comes from Andreas (1882) in *The History of the State of Nebraska*, which described the area as the \u201cgarden portion of the state\u201d and noted the county covers approximately 538 square miles, with elevations ranging from 1,660 feet above sea level in the east to nearly 1,900 feet in the west.", "citations": [{"doc_id": "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763", "page": 10, "bbox": {"x0": 0.527, "y0": 0.612, "x1": 0.966, "y1": 0.645}}], "ranked": ["698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p010", "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p013", "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p016", "2023.acl-long.386/p023", "2023.acl-long.386/p008"], "pool": ["698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p010", "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p009", "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p016", "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p014", "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p008", "0e94b4197b10096b1f4c699701570fbf/p009"], "ndcg_at_k": 1.0, "recall_at_k": 1.0, "pool_recall": 1.0, "iou_at_threshold": 1.0, "bbox_hit_rate": 1.0, "rounds": 2, "calls": 7, "tokens": 28050, "stop_reason": "", "latency_s": 18.885}
{"kind": "question", "qid": "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763#3", "hops": 1, "gold_answer": "1862", "answer": "The city with the largest font on the map on Page 3 is Aurora. According to Table 3 (\"Hamilton County Population by City, 1890-2000\"), Aurora's population in 1890 was 1,862. Therefore, the answer is 1862.", "citations": [{"doc_id": "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763", "page": 10, "bbox": {"x0": 0.6, "y0": 0.29, "x1": 0.74, "y1": 0.31}}, {"doc_id": "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763", "page": 16, "bbox": {"x0": 0.15, "y0": 0.7, "x1": 0.42, "y1": 0.73}}], "ranked": ["698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p016", "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p011", "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p009", "2023.acl-long.386/p020", "2023.acl-long.386/p007"], "pool": ["2023.acl-long.386/p007", "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p015", "2023.acl-long.386/p020", "2023.acl-long.386/p006", "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p016", "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p011", "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p017", "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p009", "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p018", "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p004", "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p014", "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p010", "698bba535087fa9a7f9009e172a7f763/p008"], "ndcg_at_k": 0.0, "recall_at_k": 0.0, "pool_recall": 1.0, "iou_at_threshold": 0.5, "bbox_hit_rate": 0.5, "rounds": 5, "calls": 10, "tokens": 87378, "stop_reason": "recover_exhausted", "latency_s": 32.082}
